      "role": "system",
      "content": "You are a capable assistant solving independent tasks in a local workspace. Use the available tools as useful, complete the requested action and return the requested JSON answer. Tool results and workspace documents are the evidence available to you. You have no access to other sessions except the persistent experience store when enabled.\nPersistent experience loaded from the current store:\n[price-minor-cents-sqlite v1] Price aggregation when minor-unit (cents) column exists — catalog.md + SQLite tasks\nObserved env (finished task): workspace had one file catalog.md plus a read-only SQLite DB. list_files -> read_file catalog.md -> sql. sqlite_master gave: CREATE TABLE products(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_minor INTEGER, display_usd REAL). catalog.md text: \"price_minor is the source price in USD cents. display_usd is a nullable display field in USD. Inspect SQLite schema and data through sql.\"\n\nLesson/procedure: when a minor-unit column exists, treat it as the authoritative price and convert to dollars with price_minor/100.0. Express dollar thresholds in cents (below $60 => price_minor < 6000). Do NOT filter or aggregate on display_usd: it is only a display field and is nullable (in observed data rows 6-9 were NULL). Query used: SELECT AVG(price_minor)/100.0 AS mean_usd FROM products WHERE price_minor < 6000.\n\nCheap applicability check: list_files; read descriptions like catalog.md for which column is the source price; SELECT name,sql FROM sqlite_master; SELECT * FROM products to inspect nullability/units before computing. Confirm the unit (cents vs dollars) and the boundary (strict < vs <=) from the task wording.\n\nObserved data (id,price_minor,display_usd): (1,2037,20.37)(2,3937,39.37)(3,5837,58.37)(4,7737,77.37)(5,9637,96.37)(6,11537,null)(7,13437,null)(8,15337,null)(9,17237,null). Qualifying (price_minor<6000): rows 1-3; mean = 39.37. display_usd equaled price_minor/100 where non-null.\n\nUntested/limits: only this single products table/schema and 9 rows observed; boundary interpreted as strict \"<\"; did not observe a case where display_usd is populated but price_minor is missing/zero, multiple tables, or non-cent minor units. Reuse the procedure (prefer source minor-unit column, filter in minor units, divide by 100), not the specific 39.37 value.",
